</p><p>For elective surgeries with a scheduled time on the daily surgical map, delays in start of anesthesia of 60 minutes or more occurred in 96 cases (71.6%).</p><p>For surgeries scheduled in the afternoon, only 14% of patients were allowed to consume breakfast and in 37.2% of them the procedure start was earlier than scheduled on the surgical map. </p><p>According to the established criteria, prolonged fasting occurred both in the preoperative and postoperative periods (<xref rid="t3" ref-type="table">Table 3</xref>). For the preoperative period, all patients remained fasting for longer than the current recommendations.</p><p>
